# boq_com_au/CHANGELOG

## 20261116

0.5.1: - BoqComAu::Account#login, #validate_args: Now uses superclass WebAccount.

1. ~ boq_com_au.gemspec: webaccount /'~> 0.9'/'~> 0.10'/
2. - BoqComAu::Account#login, WebAccount 0.10.0's naming every missing value at once.
3. - BoqComAu::Account#validate_args, WebAccount 0.10.0's being inherited.
4. ~ Account.rb's notes: login is WebAccount's.
5. ~ BoqComAu::VERSION: /0.5.0/0.5.1/


## 20261115

0.5.0: ~ BoqComAu::Account::PAGE_SELECTORS: /logged_out_xpath/logged_out_selector/, as WebAccount 0.9.0's.

1. ~ boq_com_au.gemspec: webaccount /'~> 0.8'/'~> 0.9'/
2. ~ BoqComAu::Account::PAGE_SELECTORS: /logged_out_xpath: '...'/logged_out_selector: {xpath: '...'}/, logged_out_xpath going in WebAccount 0.10.0.
3. ~ test/BoqComAu/Account_test.rb: The logged-out selector is BOQ's where none is given, and one set after construction wins over it.
4. ~ README.md: The setters win over PAGE_SELECTORS, as the keywords do.
5. ~ BoqComAu::VERSION: /0.4.1/0.5.0/

0.4.1: ~ BoqComAu::Account#login and #download_transactions name every argument missing at once, as an ArgumentError.

1. + BoqComAu::Account#validate_args
2. + BoqComAu::Account#login: Calls validate_args(username:, password:), then WebAccount#login.
3. - BoqComAu::Account#username, #password: WebAccount's readers are used, nil where not given.
4. ~ BoqComAu::Account#download_transactions: Calls validate_args(account_number:).
5. ~ test/BoqComAu/Account_test.rb: One missing and both missing are named by login, given to new or to login itself; a nil account_number is named by download_transactions; username and password are nil where not given.
6. ~ README.md, Account.rb's notes: login raises ArgumentError naming every one missing.
7. ~ Account.rb's notes: Chosen, which draws BOQ's dropdowns, is said to be a JavaScript library, as otherwise it reads as the word "chosen".
8. ~ BoqComAu::VERSION: /0.4.0/0.4.1/

0.4.0: - BoqComAu::Account#initialize: Now uses superclass WebAccount.

1. ~ boq_com_au.gemspec: webaccount /'~> 0.7'/'~> 0.8'/
2. - BoqComAu::Account#initialize, WebAccount's reading PAGE_SELECTORS itself.
3. ~ test/BoqComAu/Account_test.rb: A login page URL and a selector given win over BOQ's, the rest staying BOQ's; /logs in to BOQ, whatever else is passed to WebAccount/uses BOQ's selectors where none is given/.
4. ~ README.md: The keywords of new win over PAGE_SELECTORS.
5. ~ BoqComAu::VERSION: /0.3.0/0.4.0/


## 20261111

0.3.0: ~ BoqComAu::Account uses WebAccount 0.7.0's browser options and download waiting, so as it runs in Firefox as well as Chrome; /chrome_profile_directory:/profile_directory:/.

1. ~ boq_com_au.gemspec: webaccount /'>= 0.6.1'/'~> 0.7'/
2. ~ BoqComAu::Account#initialize: /chrome_profile_directory:/profile_directory:/; download_directory:, browser: and driver_options: go to WebAccount, as do headless:, window_size: and user_agent:.
3. - BoqComAu::Account#default_driver_options, WebAccount's giving Chrome's options or Firefox's.
4. - BoqComAu::Account#download_directory, #click, #stale?, #wait_for, #set_value, WebAccount's doing the same.
5. - BoqComAu::Account#newest_csv_filename, #wait_for_download, WebAccount's #wait_for_download waiting longer, and past Firefox's downloads in progress as well as Chrome's.
6. ~ test/BoqComAu/Account_test.rb: The tests of what's now WebAccount's are dropped; the options for Chrome and for Firefox, and profile_directory: in place of chrome_profile_directory:, are tested.
7. ~ README.md: Firefox and profile_directory:.
8. ~ BoqComAu::VERSION: /0.2.0/0.3.0/


## 20261104

0.2.0: + BoqComAu::Account#download_transactions(period:, from_date:, to_date:), choosing the dates.

1. + BoqComAu::Account::TRANSACTIONS_SELECTORS: + advanced_search_link, text_fields, search_link.
2. ~ BoqComAu::Account#download_transactions: + period: (:all, the last year, or :last_month), + from_date:, + to_date:; given any, the dates are set under Advanced Search and searched on before exporting.
3. + BoqComAu::Account#dates, #last_month_start_date, #last_month_finish_date, #formatted_date
4. + BoqComAu::Account#enter_dates: the displayed date fields set by JavaScript, so as a date picker doesn't open over them; and stops where the values didn't take, rather than exporting another range.
5. + BoqComAu::Account#search: waits for the Export All link from before the search to be replaced, else what was there before would be exported.
6. + BoqComAu::Account#set_value, #stale?, #date_fields
7. ~ BoqComAu::Transactions.download_csv_file: + period:, from_date:, to_date:
8. ~ test/BoqComAu/Account_test.rb, test/BoqComAu/Transactions_test.rb
9. ~ README.md: choosing the dates.
10. ~ BoqComAu::VERSION: /0.1.0/0.2.0/


## 20261103

0.1.0: + BoqComAu::Account#download_transactions, exporting an account's transactions as a CSV file.

1. + BoqComAu::Account::TRANSACTIONS_SELECTORS
2. + BoqComAu::Account#download_transactions(account_number:): Transaction History, the account chosen by the digits of its number, then Export All as CSV; returns the file downloaded.
3. + BoqComAu::Account#initialize(download_directory:), #download_directory: Chrome downloads there without asking, and opens nothing.
4. + BoqComAu::Account#click, #wait_for, #choose_option: a link not displayed is clicked by JavaScript; a select hidden by Chosen is chosen from by its own list, once Chosen has drawn it.
5. + BoqComAu::Account#newest_csv_filename, #wait_for_download: the file is the newest CSV since Download was clicked, rather than BOQ's name for it, which Chrome numbers where a download of the same day is there already.
6. + BoqComAu::Transactions.download_csv_file: login, download and shutdown in one, shutting down even where the download fails.
7. ~ test/BoqComAu/Account_test.rb, + test/BoqComAu/Transactions_test.rb
8. ~ README.md, boq_com_au.gemspec: downloading transactions.
9. ~ BoqComAu::VERSION: /0.0.3/0.1.0/

0.0.3: BoqComAu::Account#login is WebAccount's, which waits for the log off link.

1. - BoqComAu::Account#login, #logon
2. ~ BoqComAu::VERSION: /0.0.2/0.0.3/

0.0.2: BoqComAu::Account#shutdown is WebAccount 0.6.1's, which quits the browser even where logging out fails.

1. - BoqComAu::Account#shutdown
2. ~ boq_com_au.gemspec: webaccount >= 0.6.1
3. - test/BoqComAu/Account_test.rb: shutdown.
4. ~ BoqComAu::VERSION: /0.0.1/0.0.2/

0.0.1: ~ BoqComAu::Account#logout returns once logged off, rather than after a 30 second timeout.

1. ~ BoqComAu::Account::PAGE_SELECTORS[:logged_out_xpath]: + the Log On Again link. The page shown after logging off has no sign-in button, so logged_out? waited for one until it timed out.
2. ~ BoqComAu::VERSION: /0.0.0/0.0.1/

0.0.0: Log into and out of BOQ Classic Internet Banking.

1. + BoqComAu::Account < WebAccount: initialize(chrome_profile_directory:), login(), shutdown(), username(), password().
2. + BoqComAu::VERSION
